   "item": {
    "subject_key": "ap-calculus-ab",
    "unit_number": 2,
    "topic_code": "2.3",
    "topic_title": "Estimating Derivatives of a Function at a Point",
    "stem": "A differentiable function T gives the temperature, in °C, of a liquid t minutes after heating begins. Selected values are shown below.\n\nt (minutes): 1, 2.9, 3, 3.1, 5\nT(t) (°C): 10, 19, 20, 23, 42\n\nUsing the closest listed times on opposite sides of t = 3 to estimate T′(3), which statement is justified?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "T′(3) is approximately 8 °C/min.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Distant-data trap: (42 − 10)/(5 − 1) = 8 uses the table’s endpoints rather than the closest times surrounding 3. That slope describes change over a broader interval, not the requested local estimate. Fix: Select the nearest listed time below 3 and the nearest above 3 before computing slope."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "T′(3) is approximately 4 °C/min.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Missing-denominator trap: 23 − 19 = 4 is only the temperature change, not a rate. The elapsed time is 3.1 − 2.9 = 0.2 minute, so the change must be divided by 0.2. Fix: Divide the temperature difference by the corresponding time difference."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "T′(3) is approximately 20 °C/min.",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "The closest times surrounding 3 are 2.9 and 3.1, giving the local slope (23 − 19)/(3.1 − 2.9) = 20 °C/min. This secant slope estimates the instantaneous temperature change at t = 3."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "The table establishes that T′(3) is exactly 20 °C/min.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Estimate-as-exact trap: the nearby secant slope is 20, but finitely many table values do not determine the exact tangent slope. Differentiability alone does not make a secant slope equal the derivative. Fix: Label a derivative computed from nearby table values as an estimate, not an exact value."
     }
    ]
   },
